# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Claude Code local overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

# Generated artifacts that are NOT the V&V record
# (docs/validation_report.md IS committed -- it is the V&V artifact)
#
# docs/figures/*.png IS committed: the gallery is how the work gets explained to
# people who will not run the code, which only works if GitHub can render it.
# Everything else dropped in that directory stays local.
docs/figures/*
!docs/figures/*.png
# Self-contained shareable page: ~1.6 MB with every figure inlined as base64,
# and the bytes change on every rebuild. Regenerate it, do not version it.
docs/overview.html
# Per-scene output from scripts/run_scene.py -- regenerate it, do not version it.
runs/
*.ply
*.npy
!tests/baseline/*.npy
# Cached ray solves (RayField.save). Derived from the bathymetry and sea state,
# keyed by a hash of both, and tens of megabytes each -- regenerate, do not
# version. Listed separately from *.npy because the miss is expensive enough
# that someone will be tempted.
*.npz

# Terrain exports. Ignored as a *directory* rather than by extension: `*.npy`
# alone would leave grid_meta.json tracked on its own, and a half-committed
# export fails at load with a confusing message rather than being absent.
#
# To version one deliberately (it makes the Gate 4 checks run for everyone
# instead of skipping, at the cost of ~20 MB):
#     git add -f houdini_export/
houdini_export/
*_export/
# ... and exports that do not follow that naming. `straits*/` is a Strait of
# Hormuz export; it was briefly half-committed because `*.npy` caught the
# fields while grid_meta.json slipped through, which is the exact failure the
# note above warns about. Name new exports `<something>_export/` and they are
# covered automatically.
straits/
